Palantir’s higher annual revenue forecast confirms strong demand in another part of the AI stack (
Reuters
). It does not validate the price of every memory or equipment company. A professional test of the hardware trade is narrower: contract pricing, forward margins and the timing of customer capacity purchases. At a 4.45% Treasury 10Y, profits promised far into the buildout face a meaningful valuation hurdle. The spending cycle can remain strong while the next buyer earns less from the share.

Palantir supplies the immediate counterexample: the shares tumbled despite revenue and profit beating estimates (
Yahoo Finance
). The stronger supplier outlooks and Palantir’s negative share response highlight how demanding expectations can be within AI. The professional question is which result improves the forward case enough for the price already paid. A calmer volatility index does not reduce the operating hurdle already embedded in a demanding valuation.

Dell’s report will provide a concrete comparison for the server thesis (
Yahoo Finance
). Its customer demand, product mix and delivery costs are more useful benchmarks than assuming that two suppliers deserve the same multiple. With the Treasury 10Y at 4.48%, the timing of the owner’s return remains material. The investment test is which improved forecast still leaves an attractive payoff after the price already paid.

